the state of california just introduced  a brand new build to make bitcoin legal  tender now of course over the weekend as  this tweet started to go viral a lot of  people started to ask how do you make  bitcoin a decentralized digital currency  legal tender within a state without  having the national government sign off  on it as well well of course we started  to get more information what we saw was  that state politicians actually were the  ones who put forward this legislation  they're the ones who want to make  bitcoin legal tender what we have here  is a tweet from ian calderon who's a  state assembly member who said together  dennis porter and i are working on a  bipartisan effort to legislatively  explore bitcoin as legal tender in the  state of california more to come now i  started to go deep down the rabbit hole  i started to try to understand is this  actually real what are they talking  about well here's the senate bill itself  and what you can see is that in this  senate bill which was put forth on  february 18th of this year then all the  way down there at the bottom section one  says that they want to add to the  government code this is the change they  want to make a state agency may accept  cryptocurrency as a method of payment  for the provision of government services  that means that ultimately bitcoin would  be allowed to be accepted by those state  agencies by different departments or  groups and bitcoin would be recognized  as legal tender within the state now  this isn't the first state or government  around the world that's trying to make  this happen we know that el salvador  they already made bitcoin legal tender  last year and arizona recently  introduced a bill to make bitcoin legal  tender within their state as well but  there's also a number of countries  around the world where bitcoin is legal  for transactions france denmark germany  japan mexico spain united kingdom and  many more now the beauty of bitcoin is  it is decentralized nobody can stop you  from buying it selling it transacting in  a peer-to-peer way or simply holding it  bitcoin was built to be anti-censorship  and so ultimately we want to see  governments embracing it we want to see  them making it legal tender we want to  see it get much more beneficial tax  treatment but bitcoin is going to be  successful with or without the  government it's going to be successful  because ultimately people realize that  they want to hold a store value a medium  of exchange and a unit of account that  cannot be debased or devalued by anyone  else
 

